## Key Preferences

- External data caches (e.g., sentiment embeddings, model outputs) can silently fail through zero-filling or default values on cache miss. Row count and schema validation alone will not detect this corruption. Pre-execution validation must sample actual values across the cache range, not just verify table existence and column structure, because millions of zero-vector rows will silently corrupt training without raising any schema-level errors. (0.65 [solution])
- GDELT TimelineTone DOC API must be queried in 90-day chunks to retain daily resolution across multi-year spans. Attempting to query larger date ranges (e.g., 2018-2025 in one call) results in aggregated data loss. Per-ticker components are persisted immediately after each chunk to ensure resumability on interruption; rerunning skips completed ticker/date chunks. (0.44 [domain_fact])

